---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Coverage from '@/components/reality/Coverage.astro';
import Report from '@/components/reality/Report.astro';
import Closing from '@/components/sections/Closing.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
---

<Base
  title="Reality Check for your AI-built product"
  description="A focused human review of your AI-built product: user journeys, data, access, payments and production. Leave with evidence and a clear next move."
  ><section class="wrap page-hero">
    <div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Reality Check</div><p
      class="eyebrow"
    >
      A human review. A practical answer.
    </p><h1>Ready for real users?<br />Let's find out.</h1><p
      class="lead muted"
    >
      You've built the product. The Reality Check helps you understand whether
      it's ready for the next thing you want to do.
    </p><Button />
  </section><section class="wrap section split border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What we look at</p><h2>
        The product.<br />Not just the code.
      </h2><p class="muted mt-8">
        We agree the important journeys and risks before reviewing. A tiny beta
        and a product taking payments need different levels of confidence.
      </p><p class="notice">
        This is a product and engineering review. It is not a penetration test,
        security certification or guarantee against every failure. Specialist
        concerns get a clear referral.
      </p>
    </div><Coverage />
  </section><section class="wrap section split border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What you get</p><h2>
        Evidence.<br />Priorities.<br />Your next move.
      </h2><p class="lead muted mt-8">
        A concise report and a walkthrough of the findings. Each issue includes
        how we found it, why it matters and what to do next.
      </p><ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong>Blockers:</strong> address before the agreed next step.
        </li><li><strong>Fix soon:</strong> schedule after the blockers.</li><li
        >
          <strong>Fine for now:</strong> keep what works.
        </li>
      </ul><div class="outcomes">
        <span>Ship</span><span>Ship after fixes</span><span>Keep testing</span
        ><span>Rethink foundation</span>
      </div>
    </div><Report />
  </section><section
    class="wrap section border-t border-[var(--line)]"
    data-track-pricing
  >
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Scope before commitment</p><h2>
          Start with<br />what you've built.
        </h2>
      </div><div>
        <h3>
          {
            site.prices.check
              ? `Reality Check · €${site.prices.check}`
              : 'A fee agreed before we begin.'
          }
        </h3><p class="muted mt-6">
          Submit your product and what's coming next. We'll review the fit, then
          agree the scope, timeline and fee with you. Sending a request does not
          start a paid engagement.
        </p><Button /><h3 class="mt-12">Need help fixing it?</h3><p
          class="muted mt-4"
        >
          The optional Reality Sprint turns the priorities into a focused piece
          of work. You can also take the report and make the changes yourself.
        </p><a
          class="text-link"
          data-event="reality_sprint_clicked"
          href="/check?interest=sprint">Ask about a Reality Sprint ↗</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section><section class="wrap section border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div class="split">
      <h2>A few useful<br />answers.</h2><div>
        {
          [
            [
              'Do I need to share my repository?',
              'Not to start. A product URL and a short description are enough for the initial conversation. If code access is needed, we agree a suitable way to share it. Never send passwords or API keys in the form.',
            ],
            [
              'Will you tell me to rebuild everything?',
              'Only if the evidence supports that decision. We focus on the smallest useful set of changes for your next stage.',
            ],
            [
              'Can I keep building with AI?',
              'Yes. The findings should help you ask better questions, test the right things and keep ownership of your product.',
            ],
            [
              'How long does it take?',
              'We agree a timeline once we understand the size of the product and the journeys to review. There is no automatic audit running behind this form.',
            ],
          ].map(([q, a]) => (
            <details>
              <>
                <summary>{q}</summary>
                <p>{a}</p>
              </>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section><Closing /></Base
>
